flowchart TD
    start([Verify caller-supplied target]) --> mode{Verification mode?}
    mode -- Feature --> testing[Run required tests and review against Definition and release Design]
    mode -- Release --> eligible{All scoped features have current passing evidence?}
    eligible -- No --> blocked([Blocked: report missing evidence or unresolved cause])
    eligible -- Yes --> releaseChecks[Run integration tests and release acceptance checks]
    testing --> featureChecksPassed{Feature checks passed?}
    featureChecksPassed -- Yes --> featurePassed([Return: feature passed])
    featureChecksPassed -- No --> diagnosis[Compare findings with approved inputs and implementation]
    releaseChecks --> releaseChecksPassed{Release checks passed?}
    releaseChecksPassed -- Yes --> verificationComplete([Return: release passed])
    releaseChecksPassed -- No --> diagnosis
    diagnosis --> rootCause{Evidence identifies cause and affected targets?}
    rootCause -- Implementation defect --> implementationDefect([Return: implementation defect])
    rootCause -- Design gap --> designGap([Return: design gap])
    rootCause -- Definition change needed --> definitionChange([Return: Definition change])
    rootCause -- Unclear or external blocker --> blocked
%% @airflow-context start
%% Project supplies feature/release mode, target IDs and current approved inputs.
%% Set feature_status to verifying for feature checks; release_status to verifying
%% only for release checks. Apply the phase transitions when returning results.
%% Record check names, results, input digests and code revision or working-tree
%% evidence in .air/index.md. Return findings and affected IDs to the caller;
%% do not select the next feature or call development subflows here.

%% Feature transitions owned by this phase:
%% - `selected` -> `verifying`: Impact analysis proves existing implementation reusable; current approvals permit re-verification.
%% - `selected` -> `verified`: Impact analysis proves both implementation and passing checks unaffected by the revision.
%% - `verifying` -> `verified`: Feature acceptance checks pass against current approved inputs and code.
%% - `verified` -> `verifying`: Only checks need repeating; implementation remains valid.
%% @end-airflow-context
%% @airflow-context diagnosis
%% Diagnose from concrete evidence, not test failure alone. A Definition change
%% is a proposed requirement correction, never permission to weaken acceptance
%% criteria to fit broken code. Identify targets and invalidate affected checks
%% using Project impact rules. If cause or impact is
%% unclear, return Blocked. Project routes repair and required reapprovals.
%% @end-airflow-context
%% @airflow-context releaseChecks
%% Feature checks do not replace integration and release acceptance checks.
%% Re-run affected feature checks after repair before repeating release checks.
%% Passing checks do not authorize publication.

%% Release transition `implementing -> verifying`: All scoped features have current passing feature checks; release integration checks begin. Owner: AI, based on evidence.

%% Release transition `verifying -> release-ready`: Every feature and release-level check passes against current approved inputs. Owner: AI, based on evidence.
%% @end-airflow-context

    classDef boundary fill:#126a52,color:#ffffff,stroke:#126a52
    classDef approval fill:#fff0e8,color:#633b2c,stroke:#c68162
    class start,blocked,featurePassed,verificationComplete,implementationDefect,designGap,definitionChange boundary
